hp for OS-9/68000=================ORIG holds comp.sources.unix volume 24, hp, as posted.  The files besideit build the OS-9 program.  y.tab.c, y.tab.h and lex.yy.c were made onOS-9 from hp.gram.y and hp.scan.l with the disk's `yacc -d' and `flex -I'.What changed, and why:  hp.scan.l  The parser reads each number straight out of line[], at the  hp.c       place hp.c's reader has reached.  lex fetched characters             through that reader, input(); flex has its own input() and             reads ahead in blocks, so under OSK flex's YY_INPUT takes one             character at a time from the reader, renamed hp_input(), and             lex.yy.c is made with -I so that flex reads no further ahead             than a rule needs.  Without both, numbers were pushed wrongly             and "2 3 +" reported a stack underflow.  yyrestart() starts a             fresh scan for each line.  hp.c       The lex library, -ll on Unix, supplied yywrap(); here hp.c             does.hp.h and hp.gram.y are unchanged.Measured under os9exec: `hp 2 3 +' prints 5.000, `hp 2 10 :' 1024.000,`hp 7 2 /' 3.500, `hp 1e3 3 -' 997.000, and "2 3 + p 4 x p" on standardinput prints 5 and then 20.  Dividing by zero stops hp withE_PRCABT (Process Aborted) there.Build: cc hp.c y.tab.c lex.yy.c -DOSK -l=math.l